# Managed by Ansible (roles/ssh-hardening). Do not edit by hand.
#
# Gate 1 (Operating systems and access): SSH must be key-only with an
# explicit root policy. Verified live 2026-09-13: PasswordAuthentication no
# was already in effect globally (set by netcup's provisioning API,
# sshPasswordAuthentication=false -- not version-controlled until this role),
# but PermitRootLogin was the permissive explicit value "yes", not
# "without-password": a later change to the global PasswordAuthentication
# setting would silently reopen root to password login. Both are restated
# here explicitly. Ubuntu's /etc/ssh/sshd_config includes this directory
# first, so these values take precedence over the rest of that file.
#
# "without-password" is OpenSSH's canonical name for this setting -- "sshd
# -T" echoes it back that way even though "prohibit-password" is accepted as
# an input alias. Written here as without-password so the value in this file
# matches what verification reads back, instead of two spellings of the same
# setting.
PermitRootLogin without-password
PasswordAuthentication no
KbdInteractiveAuthentication no
PermitEmptyPasswords no
